  "description" : "FUNCTION NUMVAL's rejection half, reached the way the program reaches it. ACTIDINI carries an embedded space, so the COBOL class test at :197 - IF ACTIDINI IS NOT NUMERIC, which is true unless every character is a digit - rejects it with 'Account ID must be Numeric...' at :199-200 and the cursor at :201. The conversion at :204 is never reached, which is the point: the guard, not the intrinsic, is what an operator sees, and FUNCTION NUMVAL would have returned zero for this argument rather than refusing it. The screen echoes the value as typed, because the reject path performs no normalisation. Gate G29's full accept-and-reject table, including the currency string, the parenthesised negative, the empty argument and the all-spaces argument, is pinned directly by COTRN02CParityTest.NumericIntrinsicParity - none of those four can reach the intrinsic through this program, because the guard refuses them first.",
